# Public-facing copy

This repo is a **public website**. Visitor-facing UI must show, not tell.

## Do not

- Add explanatory subheads, helper paragraphs, or captions that document how a feature works, where data comes from (Twenty, Zotero, pipelines), or threshold rules ("at least two…", "when known").
- Expose internal system names, sync sources, or processing details in Liquid/HTML/JS UI copy.
- Write docs-style blurbs next to interactive lists, filters, or icons.

## Do

- Prefer clear labels and self-evident UI (icons, links, counts) over prose that explains the machinery.
- Put thresholds, data sources, and pipeline notes in `processing/` READMEs, code comments, or agent docs — not in the rendered page.

## Example

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD: visitor-facing docs -->
<summary>Frequent collaborators</summary>
<p>People with at least two shared works. ORCID icons come from Twenty when known.</p>

<!-- ✅ GOOD: label only; icons speak for themselves -->
<summary>Frequent collaborators</summary>
```
